WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.900
Sometimes you need to correct a value, like a typing mistake from the field.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.999
In this lesson, you will learn to change one cell, or many cells at

3
00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:16.099
once, using the row and column address, and to check every change with table.

4
00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:17.920
Let's correct some data carefully.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.014
We start again from the full Demographic table:

6
00:00:23.014 --> 00:00:25.023
three hundred fifty two rows.

7
00:00:25.023 --> 00:00:29.040
Table shows one female and three hundred fifty one males.

8
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.477
To change one cell, we use its address:

9
00:00:34.477 --> 00:00:38.449
Demographic, square brackets, row one hundred fifteen, comma, column two.

10
00:00:38.449 --> 00:00:42.420
Then the arrow, and the new value: Male, in quotes.

11
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.562
Run it, then run table again.

12
00:00:51.562 --> 00:00:54.578
Now it says Male, three hundred fifty two.

13
00:00:54.578 --> 00:00:56.840
The one female value has changed.

14
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.137
To change many cells, use a range of rows.

15
00:01:08.137 --> 00:01:12.400
Demographic, rows one colon two hundred, column two, arrow, Female.

16
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.450
Run it, and view the table.

17
00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.318
The first two hundred rows now say Female.

18
00:01:24.318 --> 00:01:28.260
Table shows two hundred female, and one hundred fifty two male.

19
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.577
This is just for practice, of course.

20
00:01:41.577 --> 00:01:46.132
In real work, you would only change a value when you know it is

21
00:01:46.132 --> 00:01:49.060
wrong, for example after checking with the field team.

22
00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.702
Let's set them back:

23
00:01:55.702 --> 00:01:58.507
rows one to two hundred, column two, Male.

24
00:01:58.507 --> 00:02:00.260
Run table again to check.

25
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:29.396
And here I change the single cell, row one hundred fifteen, back to Female.

26
00:02:29.396 --> 00:02:35.220
Table shows one female and three hundred fifty one male again, just like at the start.

27
00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.531
Finally, rows one to three hundred fifty two: every row.

28
00:03:08.531 --> 00:03:11.069
Use ranges like this with care.

29
00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:15.300
Always check with table after each change. Excellent work today!

